&nbsp;

Is there a difference between a card &quot;in play&quot; and one &quot;in a play area&quot;? &nbsp; Harvest the Mighty (I think) specifically uses the latter language, unlike Into the Stratosphere/Cedistic Dissonant. &nbsp; If so, then although the one-shots should not be counted to determine the number of cards &quot;in play&quot; (to see who Harvest&#39;s target hero will be), any one-shots that have not yet resolved and are still in a hero&#39;s &quot;play area&quot; should be suitable fodder for Harvest the Mighty. &nbsp;

&nbsp;

Sounds similar to the difference between &quot;playing a card&quot; and &quot;putting card into play&quot;; effects that prevent the former do not prevent the latter. &nbsp;

&nbsp;

